      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the guarded write path journals file state to enable rollback on failure.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before any file is overwritten, the guarded tool executor records that file\u0027s prior state (its previous content, or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n- If the agent run fails\u2014due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied\u2014the journal can roll every write back in reverse order by restoring previous content or deleting newly created files.\n- This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without needing a database transaction; the journal itself acts as a transaction log held in process memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses this rollback functionality since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5373,
      "output_tokens": 202
    }
